---
CompileFlags:
  # Eigen encapsulates openmp well so analyzing openmp adds no value. On the
  # other hand, systems don't agree on whether to put omp.h in /usr/include or
  # architecture or version-specific subdirectories, so clangd sometimes failes
  # to find omp.h. This breaks all analysis downstream of Eigen, so it's easier
  # to tell clangd to assume no parallelization whn analyzing.
  Add:
    - -DEIGEN_DONT_PARALLELIZE
    # This is a C++20 codebase (std::numbers, concepts, ...). Pin the standard so
    # clangd analyzes correctly even before a compile_commands.json exists.
    - -std=c++20
